{
  "id": "signals___adding_decibels",
  "title": "Signals - Adding Decibels",
  "description": "Calculate total signal level in decibels from multiple signal sources. Supports both equal signal levels and different signal strengths.",
  "type": "datatable",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "# Signals - Adding Decibels\n\nThe decibel (dB) is a logarithmic unit used to express the ratio of two signal values - like power, sound power or pressure, voltage, intensity etc. - where one value is a reference value.\n\n## Adding Equal Signal Levels\n\nThe total signal level in decibel from equal signal sources can be calculated as:\n\n**Lt = Ls + 10 log(n)**\n\nWhere:\n- **Lt** = total signal level (dB)\n- **Ls** = signal level from each single source (dB)\n- **n** = number of sources\n\n**Note:** Adding two identical sources (doubling the signal) will increase the total signal level by 3 dB."
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "ls",
          "label": "Signal Level from Single Source (Ls)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "dB",
          "defaultValue": 120
        },
        {
          "id": "n",
          "label": "Number of Signal Sources (n)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "sources",
          "defaultValue": 2
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "lt_equal",
          "label": "Total Signal Level (Equal Sources)",
          "formula": "inputs.ls + 10 * Math.log10(inputs.n)",
          "unit": "dB",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "datatable",
      "headers": [
        "Number of Sources",
        "Increase in Signal Level (dB)"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          2,
          3
        ],
        [
          3,
          4.8
        ],
        [
          4,
          6
        ],
        [
          5,
          7
        ],
        [
          10,
          10
        ],
        [
          15,
          11.8
        ],
        [
          20,
          13
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Adding Signals from Sources with Different Strengths\n\nThe total signal level from sources with different strengths can be calculated as:\n\n**Lt = 10 log((S1 + S2 + ... + Sn) / Sref)**\n\nWhere:\n- **S1, S2, ... Sn** = signal values (signal unit)\n- **Sref** = signal reference value (signal unit)\n\nAlternatively, if you have decibel values and a level difference:\n\n**Lt = Highest Level (dB) + Correction (dB)**"
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "ls_highest",
          "label": "Highest Signal Level",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "dB",
          "defaultValue": 120
        },
        {
          "id": "level_diff",
          "label": "Signal Level Difference",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "dB",
          "defaultValue": 3
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "lt_different",
          "label": "Total Signal Level (Different Sources)",
          "formula": "inputs.ls_highest + (inputs.level_diff <= 10 ? (inputs.level_diff === 0 ? 3 : inputs.level_diff <= 1 ? 2.5 : inputs.level_diff <= 2 ? 2 : inputs.level_diff <= 3 ? 2 : inputs.level_diff <= 4 ? 1.5 : 1) : 0)",
          "unit": "dB",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "datatable",
      "headers": [
        "Level Difference (dB)",
        "Decibels to Add to Highest Level (dB)"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          0,
          3
        ],
        [
          1,
          2.5
        ],
        [
          2,
          2
        ],
        [
          3,
          2
        ],
        [
          4,
          1.5
        ],
        [
          5,
          1
        ],
        [
          6,
          1
        ],
        [
          7,
          1
        ],
        [
          8,
          0.5
        ],
        [
          9,
          0.5
        ],
        [
          10,
          0.5
        ],
        [
          ">10",
          0
        ]
      ]
    }
  ]
}